3701
03:31:24,160 --> 03:31:25,160
 Of the nature of it.

3702
03:31:25,160 --> 03:31:26,160
 Yeah, exactly.

3703
03:31:26,160 --> 03:31:32,160
 And we might be able to anticipate, okay, we've done what we can to this point.

3704
03:31:32,160 --> 03:31:34,160
 Or the developer's done what they can.

3705
03:31:34,160 --> 03:31:39,160
 But we still anticipate the possibility to run into an issue.

3706
03:31:39,160 --> 03:31:48,160
 And, you know, so we might be letting homeowners know ahead of time, you know, that, you know, this is --

3707
03:31:48,160 --> 03:31:54,160
 Maybe you're in a brand-new development and you haven't even thought about this before.

3708
03:31:54,160 --> 03:32:02,160
 But this next season, you might want to be ready just in case, you know, as things develop.

3709
03:32:02,160 --> 03:32:05,160
 So, yeah, it could go more engineering.

3710
03:32:05,160 --> 03:32:07,160
 It could go working with the developer.

3711
03:32:07,160 --> 03:32:11,160
 It could go -- it could bump into emergency preparedness as well.

3712
03:32:13,160 --> 03:32:22,160
 So -- well, yeah, that's the next thing on my list is an emergency prep because I would like to see a new level here in our emergency prep.

3713
03:32:22,160 --> 03:32:29,160
 Now, as far as city to city goes, we do more than most cities by a good measure of --

3714
03:32:29,160 --> 03:32:30,160
 By a lot.

3715
03:32:30,160 --> 03:32:31,160
 Yeah.

3716
03:32:31,160 --> 03:32:34,160
 What about just reinstituting the DRD Hill-Lountain group?

3717
03:32:34,160 --> 03:32:37,160
 Because, like, originally when I was on council before, you gave me that assignment.

3718
03:32:37,160 --> 03:32:45,160
 And I felt like bringing -- it was Jeff and it was David Bacar with the ham radio staff.

3719
03:32:45,160 --> 03:32:51,160
 And once in a while, they'd send somebody from Sheriff and UFA and, like, different things like that.

3720
03:32:51,160 --> 03:32:54,160
 And I feel -- and there were some community members.

3721
03:32:54,160 --> 03:32:55,160
 Yeah.

3722
03:32:55,160 --> 03:33:00,160
 This is an interesting thought because -- because of the detail.

3723
03:33:00,160 --> 03:33:07,160
 Well, just here's my question as we're trying to, you know, look through this on the fly here.

3724
03:33:07,160 --> 03:33:12,160
 Is there's a lot of -- there's a lot of drilling down into details.

3725
03:33:12,160 --> 03:33:17,160
 Either it might be a category or it might be a specific area of the city.

3726
03:33:17,160 --> 03:33:19,160
 Those are details, right?

3727
03:33:19,160 --> 03:33:23,160
 Do we tie up the whole group doing that or do we bust it up?

3728
03:33:23,160 --> 03:33:25,160
 That's what I'm trying to think through.

3729
03:33:25,160 --> 03:33:26,160
 Like, for example --

3730
03:33:26,160 --> 03:33:32,160
 Like the community that has multiple responsibilities or you want the community to have very specific responsibilities?

3731
03:33:32,160 --> 03:33:33,160
 Yeah.

3732
03:33:33,160 --> 03:33:34,160
 Or does it break out?

3733
03:33:34,160 --> 03:33:38,160
 And then does it become more regional, you know, in its focus?

3734
03:33:38,160 --> 03:33:40,160
 Or does it become --

3735
03:33:40,160 --> 03:33:41,160
 Some of them --

3736
03:33:41,160 --> 03:33:42,160
 Some of them --

3737
03:33:42,160 --> 03:33:43,160
 Some of them --

3738
03:33:43,160 --> 03:33:46,160
 They already exist, though, because the whole CERT team --

3739
03:33:46,160 --> 03:33:47,160
 Yes.

3740
03:33:47,160 --> 03:33:52,160
 There's CERT areas throughout the whole city that there's a CERT leader of and they meet individually.

3741
03:33:52,160 --> 03:33:53,160
 Because, like --

3742
03:33:53,160 --> 03:33:54,160
 Yes.

3743
03:33:54,160 --> 03:33:58,160
 A CERT leader sends us a text and we all show up to the park to practice and --

3744
03:33:58,160 --> 03:34:00,160
 Two varying degrees of success.

3745
03:34:00,160 --> 03:34:01,160
 Yes.

3746
03:34:01,160 --> 03:34:02,160
 I agree with that.

3747
03:34:02,160 --> 03:34:03,160
 Yeah.

3748
03:34:03,160 --> 03:34:04,160
 You know, so some of them --

3749
03:34:04,160 --> 03:34:05,160
 Because some of the areas are better than --

3750
03:34:05,160 --> 03:34:15,160
 Like, I heard from some of our residents say, "I know we have a CERT group, but we haven't met in two years and I don't even know where we are right now."

3751
03:34:15,160 --> 03:34:16,160
 So --

3752
03:34:16,160 --> 03:34:17,160
 Yeah.

3753
03:34:17,160 --> 03:34:24,160
 Well, and I think, too, that the committee could help replace that CERT leader with someone else who's asking.

3754
03:34:24,160 --> 03:34:25,160
 I know we had --

3755
03:34:25,160 --> 03:34:26,160
 Like, guess what?

3756
03:34:26,160 --> 03:34:27,160
 You're the new CERT leader.

3757
03:34:27,160 --> 03:34:28,160
 Yeah.

3758
03:34:28,160 --> 03:34:38,160
 But maybe to your point, though, maybe the committee is the overseer of that and you have a smaller subcommittee broken out and say, "Okay, we're going to include CERT in this fund.

3759
03:34:38,160 --> 03:34:41,160
 We're going to do emergency preparedness, blah, blah, blah."

3760
03:34:41,160 --> 03:34:50,160
 They're going to meet in the subcommittee and all they're going to do is bring to us the outcome of their subcommittee so that we can high-level take it back to the city council.

3761
03:34:50,160 --> 03:34:51,160
 Yeah.

3762
03:34:51,160 --> 03:34:52,160
 Yeah.

3763
03:34:52,160 --> 03:34:53,160
 That's --

3764
03:34:53,160 --> 03:34:58,160
 That enables you to not take up, you know, senior staff and council time to all of these other committees.

3765
03:34:58,160 --> 03:35:06,160
 We can do some high-level things and then these subcommittees, which will probably be some citizens, and maybe it's not a senior staff member.

3766
03:35:06,160 --> 03:35:17,160
 Maybe it's the next level down that have been given these tasks in the specific department that could meet and do these things and kind of kick it back up, you know, upward.

3767
03:35:17,160 --> 03:35:18,160
 Yeah.

3768
03:35:18,160 --> 03:35:19,160
 Yeah.

3769
03:35:19,160 --> 03:35:20,160
 Yeah.

3770
03:35:20,160 --> 03:35:33,160
 That's the way this is kind of feeling to me is to kind of -- you have this structure, but really the structure is just to keep everything organized and on task and resourced, right?

3771
03:35:33,160 --> 03:35:36,160
 But it's really the subcommittees that are going to do all the work.

3772
03:35:36,160 --> 03:35:37,160
 Yeah.

3773
03:35:37,160 --> 03:35:38,160
 So, yeah.

3774
03:35:38,160 --> 03:35:54,160
 What it does is it allows you maybe your primary committee to take the things that are there and if we need to reach for other resources that maybe they're at the council level or they extend outside of the council level and go to a county or a regional level.

3775
03:35:54,160 --> 03:35:55,160
 Well, you certainly want to tap into those resources, right?

3776
03:35:55,160 --> 03:36:04,160
 Then that can be done by the committee to reach and bring them in there to accomplish those things and then, again, report back up to the council.

3777
03:36:04,160 --> 03:36:05,160
 Yeah.

3778
03:36:05,160 --> 03:36:06,160
 Yeah.

3779
03:36:06,160 --> 03:36:14,160
 Yeah, because definitely we want things to come to council, especially when something is identified as sort of, you know, maybe resource-like.

3780
03:36:14,160 --> 03:36:15,160
 Yeah.

3781
03:36:15,160 --> 03:36:20,160
 So there might be an adjustment to a plan somewhere or some --

3782
03:36:20,160 --> 03:36:22,160
 Overexposed in some way.

3783
03:36:22,160 --> 03:36:23,160
 Yeah.

3784
03:36:23,160 --> 03:36:24,160
 Yeah.

3785
03:36:24,160 --> 03:36:39,160
 Well, I think that committee did a good job previously, but I do agree with you with the neighborhood version of it because they do have people that do the ham stuff regionally and they do have people that go to all of the emergency planning meetings for the county.

3786
03:36:39,160 --> 03:36:43,160
 When they very first moved in, they were like some kind of captains.

3787
03:36:43,160 --> 03:36:44,160
 I don't remember what it was.

3788
03:36:44,160 --> 03:36:45,160
 Those were all --

3789
03:36:45,160 --> 03:36:46,160
 Those were all --

3790
03:36:46,160 --> 03:36:47,160
 Yeah.

3791
03:36:47,160 --> 03:36:48,160
 Those were all --

3792
03:36:48,160 --> 03:36:49,160
 Those were all --

3793
03:36:49,160 --> 03:36:50,160
 Yeah.

3794
03:36:50,160 --> 03:36:51,160
 Those were --

3795
03:36:51,160 --> 03:36:52,160
 Yeah, but those were steak led.

3796
03:36:52,160 --> 03:36:53,160
 Yeah.

3797
03:36:53,160 --> 03:36:55,160
 They checked in with and it was somebody at the city that was on the other side.

3798
03:36:55,160 --> 03:36:56,160
 Yes.

3799
03:36:56,160 --> 03:37:02,160
 And they would still do that if the steak still existed that way right now because not all the steaks are doing that.

3800
03:37:02,160 --> 03:37:03,160
 Well, no, I understand.

3801
03:37:03,160 --> 03:37:05,160
 I'm just saying that it was something that has been done.

3802
03:37:05,160 --> 03:37:06,160
 So it's not totally unfamiliar.

3803
03:37:06,160 --> 03:37:07,160
 Correct.

3804
03:37:07,160 --> 03:37:08,160
 Agreed.

3805
03:37:08,160 --> 03:37:09,160
 To keep it alive.

3806
03:37:09,160 --> 03:37:12,160
 It's something that we should because it's an organization that already exists.

3807
03:37:12,160 --> 03:37:13,160
 Yeah.

3808
03:37:13,160 --> 03:37:14,160
 You know, just --

3809
03:37:14,160 --> 03:37:15,160
 We can keep it from not dying.

3810
03:37:15,160 --> 03:37:16,160
 Yeah.

3811
03:37:16,160 --> 03:37:22,160
 Those little steak organizations because sometimes they will fade and we can keep them active.

3812
03:37:22,160 --> 03:37:23,160
 Okay.

3813
03:37:23,160 --> 03:37:25,160
 Just moving on then.

3814
03:37:25,160 --> 03:37:26,160
 This one --

3815
03:37:26,160 --> 03:37:29,160
 This one could go different directions too.

3816
03:37:29,160 --> 03:37:30,160
 This could be --

3817
03:37:30,160 --> 03:37:33,160
 End up just being sort of a housing committee.

3818
03:37:33,160 --> 03:37:38,160
 But I started out with the concept of large lot success committee.

3819
03:37:38,160 --> 03:37:46,160
 And what really drove this one to me is Scarlet Ridge.

3820
03:37:46,160 --> 03:38:03,160
 And what we need to figure out -- and this is like, you know, this would be a task for a committee -- to figure out -- because the only way that large -- we're going to have large lots is for them to be successful.

3821
03:38:03,160 --> 03:38:08,160
 And we need to know what it's going to take to make them successful.

3822
03:38:08,160 --> 03:38:11,160
 So there's going to be a little homework here.

3823
03:38:11,160 --> 03:38:19,160
 Now, like for example, we've seen and we hope to see some good successes in Firefly.

3824
03:38:19,160 --> 03:38:22,160
 But -- and there are some large lots in Firefly.

3825
03:38:22,160 --> 03:38:24,160
 It's not predominantly large.

3826
03:38:24,160 --> 03:38:27,160
 But -- but there's elements of it.

3827
03:38:27,160 --> 03:38:34,160
 And I want to make a comment about this because I want to tell you this -- there's actually something that we do within my organization for work.

3828
03:38:34,160 --> 03:38:41,160
 Where we -- when something happens, and we don't know all the details of why it happened, call it an orange tag review.

3829
03:38:41,160 --> 03:38:44,160
 But basically, we go back and we workshop from beginning to end.

3830
03:38:44,160 --> 03:38:45,160
 We started here.

3831
03:38:45,160 --> 03:38:46,160
 We got here.

3832
03:38:46,160 --> 03:38:49,160
 What were all the elements that created the impact of it?

3833
03:38:49,160 --> 03:38:52,160
 Something didn't happen the way it was supposed to.

3834
03:38:52,160 --> 03:38:57,160
 Scarlet Ridge is a good example of that because there are factors that weren't really our fault.

3835
03:38:57,160 --> 03:38:58,160
 Right.

3836
03:38:58,160 --> 03:39:00,160
 It wasn't also market fault.

3837
03:39:00,160 --> 03:39:01,160
 Right.

3838
03:39:01,160 --> 03:39:02,160
 Some of that was owner.

3839
03:39:02,160 --> 03:39:03,160
 Yes.

3840
03:39:03,160 --> 03:39:04,160
 Problems, right?

3841
03:39:04,160 --> 03:39:05,160
 True.

3842
03:39:05,160 --> 03:39:06,160
 There's a lot that falls into that scope.

3843
03:39:06,160 --> 03:39:08,160
 Trouble is another example of something like that.

3844
03:39:08,160 --> 03:39:09,160
 Right.

3845
03:39:09,160 --> 03:39:21,160
 So maybe with some of these things where you're talking about that, that could be the -- one of the responsibilities of that community is to find out why it isn't working or why we're having these problems.

3846
03:39:21,160 --> 03:39:24,160
 And then we can dig down into -- you know, because you're going to have staff members there.

3847
03:39:24,160 --> 03:39:28,160
 You're going to have, you know, people from the community there.

3848
03:39:28,160 --> 03:39:32,160
 We can go in and be honest about why this happened so we don't repeat.

3849
03:39:32,160 --> 03:39:33,160
 Yep.

3850
03:39:33,160 --> 03:39:36,160
 And then the next time around, we have success with that, right?

3851
03:39:36,160 --> 03:39:38,160
 Some of the things we're not going to be able to fix.

3852
03:39:38,160 --> 03:39:40,160
 We can't fix bad business decisions.

3853
03:39:40,160 --> 03:39:41,160
 You can't fix everything.

3854
03:39:41,160 --> 03:39:42,160
 I mean, that's out of our control.

3855
03:39:42,160 --> 03:39:47,160
 But if there are failures we can prevent, it would be awesome if we could do that.

3856
03:39:47,160 --> 03:40:05,160
 In some ways, I look at this a little bit similar to the motivations for starting the chamber, is we needed another perspective, another task force outside of the city of Morella that could approach business.

3857
03:40:05,160 --> 03:40:06,160
 Yeah.

3858
03:40:06,160 --> 03:40:14,160
 That wasn't -- because as much as a city wants to try to help a business, by the nature of the beast, you're limited, right?

3859
03:40:14,160 --> 03:40:15,160
 So --

3860
03:40:15,160 --> 03:40:17,160
 And sometimes there's conflicting interests.

3861
03:40:17,160 --> 03:40:18,160
 They are conflicting.

3862
03:40:18,160 --> 03:40:21,160
 And it's not because we want to be conflicting.

3863
03:40:21,160 --> 03:40:22,160
 Right.

3864
03:40:22,160 --> 03:40:23,160
 We're just born that way, right?

3865
03:40:23,160 --> 03:40:26,160
 We're just made that way kind of a thing.

3866
03:40:26,160 --> 03:40:27,160
 So, yeah.

3867
03:40:27,160 --> 03:40:34,160
 So, like, the chamber fills that gap in many respects that the city can't do.

3868
03:40:34,160 --> 03:40:42,160
 And thus -- well, I won't -- let Melissa talk about the successes of the chamber, but --

3869
03:40:42,160 --> 03:40:43,160
 You're sitting in them.

3870
03:40:43,160 --> 03:40:44,160
 Yeah.

3871
03:40:44,160 --> 03:40:47,160
 Let me walk you over to the hallway with a big check.

3872
03:40:47,160 --> 03:40:48,160
 Yeah.

3873
03:40:48,160 --> 03:40:49,160
 But, yeah.

3874
03:40:49,160 --> 03:41:09,160
 Like, you know, sometimes -- I just anticipate we're going to find situations where we have a well-meaning developer, but this person has great ideas, but just doesn't know how to execute and maybe could miss one secret ingredient that could mean the difference between success and failure.

3875
03:41:09,160 --> 03:41:18,160
 And this committee could help keep them pointed in the right direction so that, you know, to help make those dreams come true.

3876
03:41:18,160 --> 03:41:20,160
 And I don't know what all the factors might be.

3877
03:41:20,160 --> 03:41:32,160
 I can guess at some of them, but we really need people to drill down into this and really study it and see what we can do and what we can't do about that.

3878
03:41:32,160 --> 03:41:33,160
 So --

3879
03:41:33,160 --> 03:41:37,160
 Someone with some success with that, like Scott Hazard, might be a good one to be on there.

3880
03:41:37,160 --> 03:41:43,160
 And then maybe someone like Craig Whiting who gets that in a more regional thing.

3881
03:41:43,160 --> 03:41:44,160
 I don't know.

3882
03:41:44,160 --> 03:41:45,160
 Yeah.

3883
03:41:45,160 --> 03:41:54,160
 So it's almost kind of a mentoring thing a little bit going on there, but certainly, you know, a connection between city and developer, for sure.

3884
03:41:54,160 --> 03:41:57,160
 Another one -- oh, just venues.

3885
03:41:57,160 --> 03:41:59,160
 What -- I don't know.

3886
03:41:59,160 --> 03:42:03,160
 This maybe doesn't need to be a committee, but it certainly could be a committee.

3887
03:42:03,160 --> 03:42:08,160
 We could maybe just handle it as a council, but I don't know.

3888
03:42:08,160 --> 03:42:10,160
 It's worth considering as a committee.

3889
03:42:10,160 --> 03:42:14,160
 What venues might be the most impactful?

3890
03:42:14,160 --> 03:42:18,160
 And what should we consider first?

3891
03:42:18,160 --> 03:42:19,160
 And --

3892
03:42:19,160 --> 03:42:20,160
 Creating venues?

3893
03:42:20,160 --> 03:42:21,160
 Yes.

3894
03:42:21,160 --> 03:42:22,160
 Yeah, creating venues.

3895
03:42:22,160 --> 03:42:33,160
 You know, like for example, do we put a little bit of money into Silver Lake or do we scrap that and do something totally different?

3896
03:42:33,160 --> 03:42:34,160
 Yeah, bigger.

3897
03:42:34,160 --> 03:42:35,160
 Go bigger.

3898
03:42:35,160 --> 03:42:40,160
 But someone spending a little bit of time on that and coming back with a report.

3899
03:42:40,160 --> 03:42:54,160
 Like, for example, yeah, no, Silver Lake is good for little stuff, but if you want -- if these are your goals, we need to go bigger, and this is what we can reach if we do go bigger, and this is going to be --

3900
03:42:54,160 --> 03:43:02,160
 Maybe to your point, I mean, not to get to the end of the week with this, perhaps something that we already have, like a social camp theater.

3901
03:43:02,160 --> 03:43:23,160
 We know that it's probably too small to be an effective concert series location, but maybe it's something that we could implement with the library for them to be able to view plays and small musicals and things like that, especially during the moment months, that would enable, you know, in working even with the --

3902
03:43:23,160 --> 03:43:42,160
 with the Arts Alliance and other organizations as well that could be some of those smaller things, but we know that we want to have larger venues or where we can have concerts, where we can have pageants and things of that nature that maybe aren't going to all be inside, because we don't really have inside venues right now.

3903
03:43:42,160 --> 03:43:43,160
 Yeah.

3904
03:43:43,160 --> 03:43:44,160
 You've been to the American Fork Library.

3905
03:43:44,160 --> 03:43:45,160
 Yes.

3906
03:43:45,160 --> 03:43:47,160
 They have a little -- small theater.

3907
03:43:47,160 --> 03:43:51,160
 It's not -- it's like for those kinds of things that you're talking about.

3908
03:43:51,160 --> 03:44:12,160
 Eventually, we're going to need a much bigger theater, but for the little kids things and that kind of thing, but it's also great because if you have your legislators want to come in and talk and do an open house, there's room and it's comfortable instead of like a school setting where everybody's sitting on school chairs in a gym where they can't hear, you know, just --

3909
03:44:12,160 --> 03:44:13,160
 It could be something that we can buy into the City Hall.

3910
03:44:13,160 --> 03:44:18,160
 Well, I think that needs to be a part of the Library City Hall stuff.

3911
03:44:18,160 --> 03:44:27,160
 People just preserve it, but they -- and they'll -- they'll preserve it for businesses as well, like businesses who want to have an employee meeting and don't have a place where they can all fit.

3912
03:44:27,160 --> 03:44:31,160
 So, I agree with all the things that have been said.

3913
03:44:31,160 --> 03:44:46,160
 To me, it's a priority to make sure that we feed into the things that are already trying to bring these things to us against many uphill battles and help facilitate those instead of creating things that compete with them.

3914
03:44:46,160 --> 03:44:50,160
 So, we already have a community theater that does children's plays during the summer.

3915
03:44:50,160 --> 03:44:55,160
 I think it'd be great if we could find a way to help them get connected better with the Library and --

3916
03:44:55,160 --> 03:44:56,160
 That's kind of the way I'm looking at it.

3917
03:44:56,160 --> 03:45:02,160
 It might be a way to make them more successful by allowing the Library to be a participant in that.

3918
03:45:02,160 --> 03:45:08,160
 Well, and that's too -- when we talked about art funding, I said this is just visual right now.

3919
03:45:08,160 --> 03:45:10,160
 We should be thinking about --

3920
03:45:10,160 --> 03:45:13,160
 But perhaps they shouldn't be the same funding mechanism.

3921
03:45:13,160 --> 03:45:15,160
 Perhaps they're -- they're separate.

3922
03:45:15,160 --> 03:45:18,160
 And one is going to be -- this is the arts.

3923
03:45:18,160 --> 03:45:24,160
 And this one is going to be basically art display kind of a thing.

